<header><p class="st-kicker">crusader state · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Lordship of Arsuf</h1><p class="st-meta">1101 CE – 1265 CE · capital Arsuf</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A coastal lordship of the Kingdom of Jerusalem, near which Richard the Lionheart defeated Saladin in 1191.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arsuf">Arsuf</a>, the ancient Apollonia, surrendered to Baldwin I in 1101 with the help of a Genoese fleet. It became a lordship within the royal domain and was later granted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> families.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The lordship was small, based on a fortified town and harbour on the cliffs north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaffa">Jaffa</a>. On 7 September 1191 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england">Richard I</a> won the battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arsuf">Arsuf</a> nearby, securing the coast for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a>. In the 13th century it was held by a branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-ibelin">Ibelin family</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-of-ibelin-lord-of-arsuf">John of Ibelin</a>, lord of Arsuf and regent of the kingdom. Debts led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balian-of-arsuf">Balian of Arsuf</a> to lease it to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-hospitaller">Hospitallers</a> in 1261.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baybars">Baybars</a> besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arsuf">Arsuf</a> in 1265; after forty days the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-hospitaller">Hospitaller</a> garrison surrendered and the town was destroyed. Its ruins and castle remain at Apollonia National Park.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/lordship-of-arsuf.jpg" alt="Lordship of Arsuf" width="320" height="352"><figcaption>Image: Wikimedia Commons · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blason_Royaume_de_J%C3%A9rusalem.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1101 CE – 1265 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>crusader state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Arsuf</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>John of Ibelin, Lord of Arsuf, Balian of Arsuf</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Latin Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/israel">Israel</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Arsur</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1183&amp;focus=lordship-of-arsuf" aria-label="Lordship of Arsuf on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5575 1007 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lordship of Arsuf lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5895 1263L5908 1277M5895 1263L5815 1335"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5908 1277h0M5815 1335h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5895 1263h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5895 1263h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Arsuf. <a href="/atlas?year=1183&amp;focus=lordship-of-arsuf">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

